    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">Does Enugu get enough sun for solar?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">PVGIS modelling puts Enugu at about 1,447 kWh per kWp per year, or 3.96 kWh a day, with December the best month at 4.70 and July the weakest at 3.11. That is ahead of Lagos (1,396) and Port Harcourt (1,271) and behind Abuja (1,534). These are model figures before dust, and an installer should size the battery and panels from your own load.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">What does a 3.5 kVA solar system cost in Enugu?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">This page has no Enugu-specific price. Published October 2026 package prices from Lagos sellers put a 3.5 kVA lithium system with panels at roughly N3.1 to N3.4 million, and BusinessDay (17 February 2026) gave N2 to N3 million for 3 to 4 kVA systems. Package contents, delivery and installation differ, so a current written quote from an Enugu installer is the real number.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">Is the Enugu light tariff different from the national Band A rate?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Nairametrics reported on 21 July 2025 that the Enugu State regulator cut Band A to N160 per kWh from 1 August 2025, against N209.50 in NERC-regulated areas. Bands B to E differ by DisCo, and this page has not checked for later changes in Enugu. Read your own bill and ask the state regulator.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 10px;">How do I check that an installer in Enugu is NEMSA-certified?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Ask for their NEMSA competency certificate, then look them up in the directory at nemsa.gov.ng/directory/ or on the verification page at nemsa.gov.ng/verification/. Some Lagos sellers say they use local partners outside Lagos, so ask who will actually do the work at your house in Enugu and check that person's certificate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
